<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krishnaraja Wodeyar IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1884–1940</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Nalvadi Krishnaraja Wadiyar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Krishnaraja Wodeyar IV was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> from 1894 to 1940, ruling with full powers from 1902. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diwan">diwans</a> such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/m-visvesvaraya">M. Visvesvaraya</a> and Mirza Ismail, he made Mysore a model princely state, building dams and a hydroelectric plant, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-mysore">University of Mysore</a> and promoting industry. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a> called him a 'Rajarshi', a saintly king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krishnaraja-wodeyar-iv.jpg" alt="Krishnaraja Wodeyar IV" width="250" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nalvadi_Krishnaraja_Wodeyar_1881-1940.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
